{:edb/db-before-t 2753 :edb/db-after-t 2754 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536066 50 #inst "2026-10-09T14:12:00.377Z" 13194139536066 true] [17592186164414 1104 #edb/ref 17592186164417 13194139536066 true] [17592186166874 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381916 13194139536066 true] [17592186166874 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381930 13194139536066 true] [17592186166875 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381950 13194139536066 true] [17592186166875 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381962 13194139536066 true] [17592186167168 1017 #edb/ref 17592186164418 13194139536066 false] [17592186167168 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381909 13194139536066 true] [17592186167168 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536066 true] [17592186167168 1100 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=9x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =1\\pm 6\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." 13194139536066 true] [17592186167168 1100 "${x^{′}(t) = x(t) - 4y(t); y^{′}(t) = 9x(t) + y(t)$\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $λ = 1 ± 6\\textrm{i}$. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\nSince\n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." 13194139536066 false] [17592186167168 1145 "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that $a=\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=1>0$ and ${e}^{at}={e}^{t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, we have a spiral that is traversed toward infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0,$ the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable spiral (source)}.$" 13194139536066 true] [17592186381909 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381910 13194139536066 true] [17592186381909 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381911 13194139536066 true] [17592186381909 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381912 13194139536066 true] [17592186381909 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381913 13194139536066 true] [17592186381909 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381914 13194139536066 true] [17592186381909 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381915 13194139536066 true] [17592186381909 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139536066 true] [17592186381909 1041 "field-1" 13194139536066 true] [17592186381909 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381915 13194139536066 true] [17592186381909 1110 #uuid "0d0b049d-b68e-502e-a989-9e7aad596a89" 13194139536066 true] [17592186381910 1034 "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )<0" 13194139536066 true] [17592186381910 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536066 true] [17592186381910 1111 #uuid "29e23fb8-c1d1-5a5e-9a01-11ea7a080d79" 13194139536066 true] [17592186381911 1034 "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0" 13194139536066 true] [17592186381911 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536066 true] [17592186381911 1111 #uuid "b4e1cdac-7b2e-5f82-913e-754390960033" 13194139536066 true] [17592186381912 1034 "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=0" 13194139536066 true] [17592186381912 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536066 true] [17592186381912 1111 #uuid "ab2f15d8-137e-5dae-bbb